  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of a person, represented by their head (頁) and feet (夂), being heated underneath the sun (日). The sun component was later omitted for brevity during the Warring States period."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "中國之人也。从夊从頁从𦥑。𦥑，兩手；夊，兩足也。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Some scholars identify an oracle bone character ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 日 (“sun”) + 頁 (“head; man”) as this character – a man under the scorching sun; summer. However, it only appears as a diviner's name, making the identification uncertain.\nIn Spring and Autumn period bronze inscriptions, various variants appeared. 止 (“foot”) was often added below the man, and in some forms 日 was removed while 𦥑 (“two hands”) was added. The seal script inherits from the latter form, with 止 replaced by the related 夊.\nWarring States period forms also varied. The bamboo and silk script above shows a common form: 日 + 止 + 頁. The \"ancient script\" (古文) in Shuowen (labelled as large seal script) has deviated significantly, with 止 becoming 足 and the top part possibly a corruption of 頁.\nThe current form derives from the seal script, with 𦥑 and the legs of 頁 removed. Unrelated to 复.\n; “great; Xia Dynasty; China; Chinese”\n; “magnificent colours; variegated”"
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Sagart (2023b) relates it to 暇 (OC *[g]ˤra-s, “leisure”) and Burmese အား (a:, “to be free (not in use; without obligations)”), the latter of which STEDT derives from Proto-Sino-Tibetan *k-ra (“strength; to win; classifier for people”) but does not compare to 夏. See 暇 for more."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "中國之人也。从夊从頁从𦥑。𦥑，兩手；夊，兩足也。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "The person of 中國. Composed of 夊 'go slowly', 頁 'head', and 𦥑. Summer; Summer; 兩 (foot).",
